[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The socket path is derived from the resolved target root

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-SOCKET-IDENTITY
TITLE: The socket path is derived from the resolved target root
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The socket path is derived, never configured, so a server and a client that
never met agree on it.

The target root resolves from --root, else SCRIBE_ROOT, else by walking up from
the current directory for strictdoc_config.py. The socket is then named under
the user runtime directory from that resolved absolute path: a readable slug
plus a short digest of the path, so a directory listing is legible to a person
while remaining collision-proof and stable across a branch rename.

DEVENV_STATE is deliberately not the lookup. It is set only inside a devenv
shell, and the most frequent client -- an agent invoking the binary by absolute
path with no shell -- would compute a different answer from the server.
<<<
